This is...

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:18.100
Until the next election, which is about two years.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:22.580
If he makes it, I don't know.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:25.480
Sharon seems to be a very intelligent person.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.580
I will not...

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:31.360
What?

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:34.640
He is not inflammatory.

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:38.640
The ones who are inflammatory are the left.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:44.400
The left in Israel are fanatic Bolshevik.

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:51.260
I mean, they are really, and they call them, they call them fascists, they call them Nazis, they call them this.

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:55.420
For them, and no matter what he does, the way he says.

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:56.340
You can't call someone a Nazi.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:56.620
What?

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:58.860
In America, you can't call someone a Nazi.

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:02.200
Well, in Israel, you cannot call somebody a Nazi.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.740
If you are from the right wing, you cannot call the left wing a Nazi.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:08.040
But if you are on the left wing, you could call.

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.260
Yes, alright.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:13.560
Going to an example.

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:16.440
Look, imagine in America,

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:24.960
if a judge would say that the religious people are like lice and vermin,

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:26.840
that they should be exterminated.

00:07:27.100 --> 00:07:30.880
This was said by a judge in Israel about the religious people.

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:34.100
Now, when it came to the time for promotion,

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:37.960
the chief justice of Israel wanted to do a promotion.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:42.040
Finally there was a whole claim on how the guy is a racist.

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:46.040
He's a Jewish racist against religious people.

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:53.040
You could say I don't like religious people, but you cannot call them lice and vermin that should be exterminated.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:08:00.040
Imagine if religious people would say this about secularists.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:07.040
Israel still has a long time before becoming a true democracy.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:10.040
you know, let's speak about something more important than that.

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:20.040
You see, our Torah, we view the Torah, for instance, from a religious point of view,

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:24.040
and it's very nice, for instance, I put up a linn,

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:33.040
don't work on Shabbat, we pray, we eat kasher, and this beautiful, wonderful things.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:40.040
But sometimes we overlook the fact that the Torah enlightened humanity.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:48.040
If there is anything worthwhile in humanity today, it didn't come not from the Greeks and not from the Romans.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:51.040
It came from us, from our side.

00:08:51.040 --> 00:09:03.120
And I want to begin by pointing out something terribly, terribly simple and profound at the same time.

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:10.220
Well, I'd like to see your father in some time.

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:11.740
How is he doing?

00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:12.760
Very well.

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:13.260
Wonderful.

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:14.800
Does he go to his office?

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:16.860
He goes to work?

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:20.460
He comes back from Florida every few weeks to check on the office.

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:22.320
That's cool. That's the way to do it.

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:26.540
But you're going to be in Florida? You should go visit it.

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:28.040
Thank you. Thank you very much.

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:29.420
Are you going to be in Florida for a week?

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:30.100
Just for a week.

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:33.160
You're literally 10 minutes from Hollywood.

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:36.720
All right. I will try to.

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:39.020
Thank you. Thank you very much.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:39.840
Thank you.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:48.360
So I want to explain something about the whole idea of

00:09:48.360 --> 00:10:01.860
If I would ask you what is the difference between believing that there is only one God

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:08.700
who created everything and more than one God, what's the difference?

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:24.840
I mean, not what is the truth, but how does it make in our lives, in our mind, a difference whether there is one God or there are many gods?

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:27.100
I mean, to the simple person.

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:30.600
Do you understand the question that I'm asking?

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:36.480
I mean, I'm not talking about the philosopher or the theologian or the Kohen or the Kohanim.

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:40.480
you and me

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:42.160
the same for people

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:45.000
what I am going to point out

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.600
is that the difference is enormous

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:48.200
enormous

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:51.020
and that was a true revolution

00:10:51.020 --> 00:10:53.060
affected by the Torah

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:55.600
and it explains

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:57.300
something very very simple

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:59.320
in antiquity

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:01.860
outside the realm of Torah

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:04.020
there were many gods

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:06.000
it doesn't mean there were many gods

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:13.000
It means, first of all, that things in life do not jive.

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:23.000
What I want to say, which is strange to us today, because we have Israel and even the

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:28.000
they've been under 200 years of, 300 years of modernity.

00:11:30.380 --> 00:11:34.460
But for a Greek or for a Roman,

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:37.860
if he's walking and he sees a breeze,

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:39.940
you never saw a relationship, I say,

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:44.940
between the breeze, the waves on the lake,

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:50.300
the vibration of a flower,

00:11:53.000 --> 00:12:01.000
storm, big wind and then rain, rain and then things that grow.

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:09.000
For the ancient person every phenomenon is separate from the other.

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:15.000
There is no unity, things are in fractions.

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:23.000
One of the greatest Hiddushim in the history of humanity is Mashivaluwa Homonidakesha.

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:37.000
The simple notion that there is a connection between the wind that blows and the rain that falls was strange to the common person in antiquity.

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:51.000
They didn't see relationships. A polytheistic mind focused just on specific data cannot connect the things.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:13:02.000
Now, very good. There is no connection. There are many gods. How things happen?

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:12.000
Well, they happen because the god fights and one or two or X amount of gods overpower the other.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:16.000
Which means here comes a very important thing.

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:25.000
Violence is the means by which things operate.

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:29.000
There is always a question of fighting.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:34.000
We say in the Tefillin something which nobody pays attention to.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:38.000
O se shalom bimromav.

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:43.000
We believe, we are one of the first people in the world

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:48.000
who believe that all these different forces are in harmony

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:51.000
and God O se shalom bimromav.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:57.000
So if you believe that there are many gods,

00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:03.000
then things could be resolved only through force.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:07.000
If you believe that there is one God,

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:12.000
it means that there is harmony in the world.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:15.000
Of course you have to see how to connect,

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:18.000
the simple connection,

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:21.000
chidush kadol, maschiva ruach,

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:24.000
umo edukation, simply like this.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:36.000
In antiquity, for instance, we speak about medicine, but medicine was effected through magic.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:42.000
The doctors in antiquity didn't perform operations.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:49.000
I mean, what they were, the words were the most important thing for a Roman doctor.

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:55.000
the first thing that they would ask you is under what sign you were born.

00:14:55.000 --> 00:15:00.000
And they would try to make all kinds of incantations.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:07.000
It was only when we discovered, first is Jesus,

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:13.000
Jesus, if you look into the Christian scriptures,

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:21.700
what is true of his being divine was that he performed magic things

00:15:21.700 --> 00:15:24.160
and he cured the sick, yes?

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:28.740
And until now we have in America a very strong tradition of evangelists

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:36.440
who try to emulate, going to the end, to make the same face as the master,

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:41.540
all those things, but the whole notion that

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:44.540
but we have to be a part of it

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:49.540
we have an obligation

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:56.540
to try to cure something through natural means

00:15:56.540 --> 00:15:58.540
this is what we chose

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:01.540
by the way, in the Talmud is the first place

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:03.540
and we will wait

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:06.540
hello, you doing yours or you doing mine?

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:07.540
what is this?

00:16:07.540 --> 00:16:09.540
what's KTU Clubhouse?

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:11.540
I'm done right now, look!

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:13.540
I can do six things at once.

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:17.540
Oh my god.

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:29.540
Three. Four.

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:33.540
Five.

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:37.540
Six, seven.

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:39.240
No, they are not good.

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:40.180
Is it yours?

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:41.720
No, I don't have that.

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:52.060
That's all I can see.

00:16:52.060 --> 00:17:10.540
So I wanted to say the first thing is that

00:17:10.540 --> 00:17:14.540
believing in one single God

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:19.720
opened the mind of the people

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:22.460
and they look into the universe

00:17:22.460 --> 00:17:24.540
into a different way.

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:28.080
When today we may make an experiment on Earth,

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:31.280
we see that the same results,

00:17:31.560 --> 00:17:33.500
theoretically and in practice,

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:38.120
apply to the entire universe.

00:17:38.420 --> 00:17:42.160
That is the way today we are understanding the universe

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:46.720
because we assume that whatever experiment is in this planet,

00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:49.160
the same laws of nature

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:52.780
more or less, yes, following a kind of a logic,

00:17:53.060 --> 00:17:58.380
logic of nature, will apply into the rest of the universe.

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:00.480
Otherwise we would not know nothing,

00:18:00.920 --> 00:18:06.000
which proves, yes, the whole basis of Judaism,

00:18:06.320 --> 00:18:09.080
that the whole universe, yes,

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:13.620
is the creation of a single God.

00:18:14.140 --> 00:18:14.320
Point.

00:18:15.080 --> 00:18:15.900
No violence.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:16.600
All right.

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:18.660
Here comes another point.

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:37.460
The Yamanai says something very, very, very, the Mishnah rather, says something very, very, very, very, that when the people, somebody wanted to testify about a criminal, somebody committed a crime, it's a criminal law.

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:54.860
So they warned each witness about the consequences and one of the thinkers said everybody created in the image of God and we are all created under this one God, we are all the same.

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:56.880
And then he says something very interesting.

00:18:57.760 --> 00:19:01.060
You know why God wanted all of us,

00:19:01.220 --> 00:19:02.260
the process of God,

00:19:02.340 --> 00:19:03.560
in the image of God?

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:06.840
Because we should not be like the meaning.

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:12.560
What is the theory of,

00:19:13.160 --> 00:19:14.920
the theology of the meaning?

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:17.640
The theology of the meaning is

00:19:17.640 --> 00:19:19.160
that there are many gods.

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:20.360
So what?

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:21.320
There are many gods.

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:25.480
your God is not my God

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:28.940
my God

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:31.420
is better than your God

00:19:31.420 --> 00:19:34.280
for instance among the Greeks

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:38.720
they believed that there was one God who creates men

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:41.580
and one God who creates women

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:46.300
if we are not created by the same God

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:50.240
then there is no possibility

00:19:50.240 --> 00:19:52.880
ever of having peace.

00:19:53.940 --> 00:19:58.360
There is an intrinsic difference between us.

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:01.340
If I kill somebody

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:04.980
who is from a different god, who is that woman?

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:10.240
Well, that is not the same Avon

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:14.160
as if I kill somebody who is under my god.

00:20:14.820 --> 00:20:18.280
So, what I wanted to say just now is that the whole

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:24.100
idea of Shema Yisrael Adonai Eloheinu Adonai Yachad we could call it religious and it is

00:20:24.100 --> 00:20:31.240
religious of course it has all religious implications but it opened the mind and

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:40.860
therefore humanity as a consequence it start focusing in a different way

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:50.280
and the other step in the Torah to have a wonderful wonderful metaphor that the

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:57.140
universe the whole alarm is a book written by God

00:20:57.140 --> 00:21:05.840
It is a cosmic book.

00:21:07.380 --> 00:21:09.620
Well, if you write only one letter,

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:15.080
you will not know what the rest of the book is saying.

00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:21.500
The only way to know what the book says

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:26.100
is to know it in its totality.

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:32.140
And that's a very difficult task.

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:41.140
Out of this idea, the first scientific mind emerged.

00:21:41.140 --> 00:21:45.140
And I've written about him now because I like him very much.

00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:53.140
He was a Jew who left Spain and because his parents rather left Spain,

00:21:53.140 --> 00:22:01.140
He was born in France. His name was Sanchez. And he wrote the first scientific book.

00:22:01.140 --> 00:22:11.140
Out of this, out came out, you know. In 15, around 1552, he wrote, he published a book,

00:22:11.140 --> 00:22:17.140
The Revolution of the World. It's called the book, I wrote it in Latin.

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:19.500
He says that nothing can be known.

00:22:21.200 --> 00:22:22.860
That's the name of the book.

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:26.120
Nothing can be known.

00:22:26.120 --> 00:22:27.480
But it's very well said.

00:22:28.260 --> 00:22:29.940
It's great.

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:38.160
He says, by the way, I was the first one to decipher the book.

00:22:39.680 --> 00:22:42.880
What needs to be done in Latin.

00:22:42.980 --> 00:22:44.620
I deciphered the book.

00:22:45.020 --> 00:22:45.360
Why?

00:22:45.360 --> 00:22:50.960
because he says something and on the side it says Matthew,

00:22:51.620 --> 00:22:55.120
the book of Matthew, Matthew, the half-word is.

00:22:56.120 --> 00:22:57.280
It's not in Matthew.

00:22:58.480 --> 00:23:00.300
It is in Lambam, in Merem-e-Bukim.

00:23:00.820 --> 00:23:04.540
But who would say that it's in Merem-e-Bukim because the word burn him?

00:23:04.880 --> 00:23:06.020
Why did you write it in Latin?

00:23:06.540 --> 00:23:09.940
No, because that was the scientific language at the time.

00:23:10.660 --> 00:23:12.060
Yes, you write it in Latin.

00:23:12.060 --> 00:23:18.800
So, but on the side, so when I read it, I said, this comes from Arambam.

00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:22.180
Then I said, maybe I made a mistake and I checked it out.

00:23:22.280 --> 00:23:23.740
Maybe Arambam took it from Matthew.

00:23:24.220 --> 00:23:25.200
So I read this.

00:23:26.280 --> 00:23:35.720
And then I noticed that whenever he puts a haqqam, he would put on the side, I don't know, something like a Corinthian, whatever it is.

00:23:37.040 --> 00:23:39.380
Very, very, because no, he could not do it.

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:40.660
It was a question of the Hashem.

00:23:40.660 --> 00:23:45.660
Now, a very, very interesting thing.

00:23:45.660 --> 00:23:55.660
Now, it comes out, I am not saying it is very clear, to know one single point perfectly,

00:23:55.660 --> 00:24:00.660
you should have to know the entire system.

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:06.660
Moreover, you should have to know also the way your brain works.

00:24:06.660 --> 00:24:18.660
It allows you to see the thing way. It's impossible. That is the point of Sanchez, who are near situ. You cannot know nothing.

00:24:18.660 --> 00:24:29.660
Out of this premise came out the most brilliant scientific theory. Let's see if you can tell me. We cannot know anything.

00:24:29.660 --> 00:24:39.660
know anything. So, therefore, before that, 1550, 1552, something like that.

00:24:39.660 --> 00:24:42.660
So is there a method?

00:24:42.660 --> 00:24:48.660
But before Roger Bacon, 100 years before Roger Bacon,

00:24:48.660 --> 00:24:52.660
it was a simple idea. We didn't know everything.

00:24:52.660 --> 00:24:58.660
To know something, and this he took it from Madame Pomme,

00:24:58.660 --> 00:25:00.660
You have to create it.

00:25:02.980 --> 00:25:05.820
God knows everything, according to Aramban,

00:25:06.600 --> 00:25:08.120
because he created everything.

00:25:09.660 --> 00:25:09.920
All right?

00:25:10.800 --> 00:25:17.560
Now, true knowledge is a consequence of creation.

00:25:17.980 --> 00:25:19.040
Let me give you an example.

00:25:19.400 --> 00:25:22.600
Suppose you write a letter to your wife.

00:25:23.660 --> 00:25:26.240
You know exactly what this letter means, correct?

00:25:26.900 --> 00:25:27.240
Why?

00:25:27.240 --> 00:25:30.060
because you created that letter.

00:25:32.340 --> 00:25:35.480
Knowledge is a consequence of creation.

00:25:36.780 --> 00:25:37.960
That's why Arambam says,

00:25:38.420 --> 00:25:40.860
God created everything out of nothing.

00:25:41.280 --> 00:25:41.660
Why?

00:25:42.260 --> 00:25:45.660
Because if he created everything out of something,

00:25:46.300 --> 00:25:47.980
then it means that that something,

00:25:48.100 --> 00:25:49.200
he doesn't know it perfectly.

00:25:51.200 --> 00:25:53.400
God knows everything perfectly

00:25:53.400 --> 00:25:55.460
because he created everything.

00:25:55.460 --> 00:26:03.460
That's why in Judaism we don't say that there was something eternal and God changed it and made it into whatever it is.

00:26:03.460 --> 00:26:10.460
No. Because then that something, since it's not created by God, cannot be known.

00:26:10.460 --> 00:26:18.460
Out of this came out something which is called for the first time, I say that this is the first time it appears in the,

00:26:18.460 --> 00:26:22.720
in the, he calls it in Latin modus siendi.

00:26:22.960 --> 00:26:24.100
You know what modus siendi means?

00:26:24.440 --> 00:26:25.600
Scientific methodology.

00:26:26.460 --> 00:26:27.060
It's like this.

00:26:27.880 --> 00:26:28.280
Look at it.

00:26:30.380 --> 00:26:33.640
The only way to know is by creating it.

00:26:34.460 --> 00:26:36.700
That's what we have to know.

00:26:37.140 --> 00:26:43.860
By making experimentations, you take something, you change it,

00:26:43.860 --> 00:26:47.340
and through the change that we affect

00:26:47.340 --> 00:26:51.860
we know that experimentation

00:26:51.860 --> 00:26:55.460
and he believed that experimentation

00:26:55.460 --> 00:26:59.760
has to be through a mathematical theory which he speaks about

00:26:59.760 --> 00:27:03.780
mathematics enable me to measure

00:27:03.780 --> 00:27:07.800
the changes that I am affecting

00:27:07.800 --> 00:27:10.600
and what I know, I don't know everything

00:27:10.600 --> 00:27:35.680
I know this particular thing and I know it because I created it. Now, our knowledge is different than the knowledge of God because God created everything. I created that particular phenomenon, yes, out of substance which still was created by God, yes.

00:27:35.680 --> 00:28:01.260
But here we have the first step to scientific knowledge. You must create to know. Knowledge is the effect of creating. We make experimentations and experimentations enable us not to be like God.

00:28:01.260 --> 00:28:05.340
but to imitate God.

00:28:06.660 --> 00:28:09.740
So here we have something interesting, you know,

00:28:10.400 --> 00:28:13.880
that this is a scientist, yes.

00:28:14.460 --> 00:28:19.500
And then out of that came out a goal.

00:28:19.600 --> 00:28:20.060
He said something.

00:28:20.160 --> 00:28:21.380
I'll come to it in a minute.

00:28:22.820 --> 00:28:27.240
He goes to something and we'll speak about it in a second.

00:28:27.240 --> 00:28:44.940
But he wanted to introduce to us that it's not only that we brought the religion into the world, which is true, we brought the true religion, but only I mean we enlightened the world.

00:28:44.940 --> 00:28:47.540
You know, it's a simple idea.

00:28:47.540 --> 00:28:51.340
I mean, simple ideas that revolutionize the world.

00:28:51.340 --> 00:28:59.940
Now, out of this, a god, very intelligent god,

00:28:59.940 --> 00:29:02.940
was O'Hare Israel, and I speak always about him,

00:29:02.940 --> 00:29:05.340
the God, his name was .

00:29:05.340 --> 00:29:07.840
Now he's famous.

00:29:07.840 --> 00:29:11.940
He says, no, no, in the last, no, no, not that,

00:29:11.940 --> 00:29:14.040
he's famous, the guy is famous.

00:29:14.040 --> 00:29:17.420
And I am supposed to be an expert.

00:29:17.600 --> 00:29:20.160
Whenever there's something ambiguous, invite me to read the paper.

00:29:20.160 --> 00:29:22.960
I like him very much because he's O'Hare Israel.

00:29:24.200 --> 00:29:32.700
And I believe that when a non-Jew is O'Hare Israel, we don't have too many.

00:29:32.980 --> 00:29:34.720
Yes, so we should, you know.

00:29:35.400 --> 00:29:42.180
He died, he was born in the 1680s or 1670s, and he died in 1700 and so on.

00:29:42.180 --> 00:29:48.180
And I write a lot about him because again, he's an Irish writer and we should...

00:29:48.180 --> 00:29:53.180
But he came up with an idea and I show in one of my writings the idea came up.

00:29:53.180 --> 00:29:59.180
It came written by Vico, it comes from Sanchez. And what is the idea?

00:29:59.180 --> 00:30:08.180
It is pretty... You know, in the West we have science and we have the humanities.

00:30:08.180 --> 00:30:19.180
poetry, literature, art, music, theater, what have you, history, humanity.

00:30:19.180 --> 00:30:30.180
Rico says the following, science we cannot know perfectly because we don't read everything in science.

00:30:30.180 --> 00:30:36.180
Even the subatomic things are still there, they are, you know, whatever experiment,

00:30:36.180 --> 00:30:43.180
you know, now we have the smashers and so on, they change the things, but still you don't create anything out of nothing.

00:30:43.180 --> 00:30:47.180
But there is something that we create out of nothing.

00:30:47.180 --> 00:30:57.180
In this literature, the humanities, and therefore says, there is a place for the study of humanities,

00:30:57.180 --> 00:31:02.180
because that is the creation of the human spirit.

00:31:02.180 --> 00:31:22.180
So for the first time we have now a very beautiful demarcation between the science that we know through experimentation and the humanities which is out of creation, is out of creation almost out of nothing.

00:31:22.180 --> 00:31:24.180
Alright, wow.

00:31:24.180 --> 00:31:31.180
But this goes back to the whole notion which is written in the Gemara, is written in the Torah,

00:31:31.180 --> 00:31:37.180
that the world is a book written by Borei Olam.

00:31:37.180 --> 00:31:44.180
When Moshe Rabbeinu wanted to say to God, kill me, how did he say to God, kill me?

00:31:44.180 --> 00:31:53.300
And the Chagamin say because the serpent that God wrote is the world.

00:31:54.780 --> 00:31:57.320
We write with ink or with this.

00:31:57.740 --> 00:31:59.120
That's the way God writes.

00:31:59.380 --> 00:32:02.160
This is the way God writes.

00:32:02.420 --> 00:32:03.720
And star and so on.

00:32:03.760 --> 00:32:04.800
This is the way he writes.

00:32:06.000 --> 00:32:09.840
Now, here now you're going to understand the truth.

00:32:11.040 --> 00:32:13.100
When I say the true Kabbalah, I don't mean the Hasid Shalom,

00:32:13.100 --> 00:32:21.200
the other Kabbalah, but the true understanding of the Kabbalah, of Jewish mysticism.

00:32:22.940 --> 00:32:32.520
If the world is a book, it means that everything must be meaningful.

00:32:34.620 --> 00:32:38.480
And that is the difference between the Jew and the Greek.

00:32:38.480 --> 00:32:39.920
That is the difference.

00:32:41.340 --> 00:32:42.860
Forget about what I said.

00:32:43.100 --> 00:32:58.100
Let's take this object. Let's look at it as an object. If this is an object, it doesn't mean anything. It is what it is.

00:32:58.100 --> 00:33:01.980
but if this is not an object

00:33:01.980 --> 00:33:03.940
it is a letter

00:33:03.940 --> 00:33:09.500
then you say

00:33:09.500 --> 00:33:12.880
maybe I want to connect this letter

00:33:12.880 --> 00:33:15.500
with this letter

00:33:15.500 --> 00:33:20.980
and out of this connection

00:33:20.980 --> 00:33:25.260
a meaning will emerge

00:33:25.260 --> 00:33:28.820
whether this is an object

00:33:28.820 --> 00:33:30.600
or this is

00:33:30.600 --> 00:33:33.040
or a letter

00:33:33.040 --> 00:33:38.120
the difference is whether there is meaning in the world

00:33:38.120 --> 00:33:42.520
or the world is not meaningful

00:33:42.520 --> 00:33:46.300
objects do not mean

00:33:46.300 --> 00:33:48.840
but letters

00:33:48.840 --> 00:33:51.840
or thought

00:33:51.840 --> 00:33:54.520
which are not being made

00:33:54.520 --> 00:33:56.360
not only Mopetim

00:33:56.360 --> 00:33:58.360
but Otot

00:33:58.360 --> 00:33:59.860
and what does it mean the word Ot?

00:34:02.040 --> 00:34:02.620
it means

00:34:02.620 --> 00:34:03.560
a letter

00:34:03.560 --> 00:34:06.260
and means also a miracle

00:34:06.260 --> 00:34:08.720
the miracle of God

00:34:08.720 --> 00:34:10.760
is an Ot

00:34:10.760 --> 00:34:14.740
he is writing you

00:34:14.740 --> 00:34:16.100
he is telling you

00:34:16.100 --> 00:34:17.000
something

00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:20.740
is this a meaningful

00:34:20.740 --> 00:34:22.580
world or is

00:34:22.580 --> 00:34:26.380
a world that things are and just are.

00:34:27.600 --> 00:34:30.320
That is the difference between

00:34:30.320 --> 00:34:34.040
the Greek mind and the Jewish mind.

00:34:34.900 --> 00:34:38.880
Because the Jews saw the universe as a book

00:34:38.880 --> 00:34:41.460
always looked into

00:34:41.460 --> 00:34:43.840
interrelationships

00:34:43.840 --> 00:34:50.800
and the meaning behind the things.

00:34:50.800 --> 00:35:02.800
The ultimate, of course, knowledge of anybody is if you could read a single line of what Borei Olam wrote.

00:35:02.800 --> 00:35:12.800
I give once an example, and you're going to see the difference between the Jewish Chachamim and the Greek Chachamim.

00:35:12.800 --> 00:35:20.300
Yes. Suppose something comes, I don't know, a meteorite just drops into planet Earth.

00:35:21.400 --> 00:35:29.260
You see some marks. There's two ways how to investigate this meteorite.

00:35:30.260 --> 00:35:38.200
You could look into the chemistry of the meteorite,

00:35:38.200 --> 00:35:46.200
analyze the components of the stone or whatever it is, and disregard the marks.

00:35:46.200 --> 00:35:49.200
That is the Greek way.

00:35:49.200 --> 00:35:58.200
Maybe the marks are a special kind of writings.

00:35:58.200 --> 00:36:07.200
And if the marks are writing, then the chemical composition of this meteorite

00:36:07.200 --> 00:36:15.200
is totally unimportant. In other words, if I send you something and you receive it and you think that it is a letter,

00:36:15.200 --> 00:36:25.200
it's not important whether the ink is red, brown, blue, black, or what is the composition of the paper.

00:36:25.200 --> 00:36:30.200
You don't start analyzing the material composition, the physical composition of the paper.

00:36:30.200 --> 00:36:31.900
you want to read the letter.

00:36:33.540 --> 00:36:37.080
But if you think that the writing is unimportant,

00:36:39.240 --> 00:36:41.640
then the only thing that you do is you get the letter

00:36:41.640 --> 00:36:43.420
and put it on the microscope.

00:36:45.800 --> 00:36:47.320
That is the difference.

00:36:49.540 --> 00:36:51.200
Yes, that is the difference.

00:36:52.200 --> 00:36:52.440
Yes.

00:36:52.740 --> 00:36:55.460
If you think that the letter, there's no such thing as writing.

00:36:56.460 --> 00:36:56.760
Yes.

00:36:56.760 --> 00:37:10.760
And then if there is something, the letter, the only thing you can do with the letter is to observe the chemical and physical properties of the paper or of the ink.

00:37:10.760 --> 00:37:22.760
But if it is writing, then you have to discover the meaning of the letter.

00:37:22.760 --> 00:37:29.760
Again, is the world, the universe meaningful or not?

00:37:29.760 --> 00:37:36.760
Is it the writing of Paul Holland or is it just like that?

00:37:36.760 --> 00:37:40.760
Just like that, just like that.

00:37:40.760 --> 00:37:47.760
I once wrote a paper, a very interesting paper, in English I wrote it.

00:37:47.760 --> 00:37:50.460
It's called God as a writer.

00:37:52.080 --> 00:37:53.160
Because in the Torah,

00:37:54.360 --> 00:37:55.180
in the whole universe,

00:37:55.320 --> 00:37:56.600
is the writing of a gospel.

00:37:57.080 --> 00:37:59.160
That's the self-referential God.

00:37:59.620 --> 00:38:01.640
They do two kinds of books.

00:38:02.260 --> 00:38:03.600
One very, very big,

00:38:04.180 --> 00:38:04.700
the cosmos,

00:38:05.240 --> 00:38:05.900
and they're small.

00:38:06.200 --> 00:38:07.940
The Torah and the complement each other.

00:38:08.140 --> 00:38:08.920
God is a writer.

00:38:09.740 --> 00:38:10.260
Interesting.

00:38:10.740 --> 00:38:11.500
For the Greeks,

00:38:12.740 --> 00:38:14.040
I pointed out,

00:38:15.160 --> 00:38:16.440
for the Greeks,

00:38:16.440 --> 00:38:20.620
none of the gods of the Greeks know how to write.

00:38:23.140 --> 00:38:26.380
The Greek gods do not know how to write

00:38:26.380 --> 00:38:29.720
and do not know how to read. In the whole Greek mythology,

00:38:30.580 --> 00:38:33.540
there's not one case in which a god read something.

00:38:34.440 --> 00:38:36.980
Interesting, no? And then I put it out there.

00:38:36.980 --> 00:38:41.000
They are wonderful gods, but they are

00:38:41.000 --> 00:38:43.480
with all due respect, illiterate.

00:38:43.480 --> 00:38:52.480
Now more than that, Plato thought that writing is falsification.

00:38:52.480 --> 00:39:00.480
One step further, for us the most honorable profession that a person could have is what?

00:39:00.480 --> 00:39:04.480
In the time of the Gemara and the Mishnah, sofer.

00:39:04.480 --> 00:39:12.480
For the Greeks to be a sofer is a dishonorable profession.

00:39:12.480 --> 00:39:13.420
Interesting, no?

00:39:15.000 --> 00:39:16.500
Writing is not important.

00:39:18.420 --> 00:39:20.420
Only because you're going to forget

00:39:20.420 --> 00:39:22.500
and that and that, you write

00:39:22.500 --> 00:39:24.360
as a necessity.

00:39:25.240 --> 00:39:26.500
But writing

00:39:26.500 --> 00:39:27.080
per se

00:39:27.080 --> 00:39:29.200
is not important.

00:39:29.940 --> 00:39:32.080
So here you have, again, two different

00:39:32.080 --> 00:39:33.760
ideas, alright?

00:39:34.680 --> 00:39:36.400
But there is something more than that.

00:39:37.840 --> 00:39:38.520
The world

00:39:38.520 --> 00:39:40.760
is what? A book for us.

00:39:41.140 --> 00:39:42.000
God is what?

00:39:42.480 --> 00:39:54.480
the writer. Question. Is there any relationship, any physical relationship between Mr. Shakespeare

00:39:56.320 --> 00:39:58.800
and Romeo and Juliet?

00:40:02.240 --> 00:40:09.120
I'm asking you. Is there any physical relationship between Mr. Shakespeare and Hamlet?

00:40:09.120 --> 00:40:14.120
How are you defining physical relationship?

00:40:14.120 --> 00:40:17.120
Whatever it is, something that you could put in a microscope.

00:40:17.120 --> 00:40:18.120
No.

00:40:18.120 --> 00:40:20.120
No. I ask you one question.

00:40:20.120 --> 00:40:23.120
How did Shakespeare create the Hamlet?

00:40:23.120 --> 00:40:26.120
Out of something or out of nothing?

00:40:26.120 --> 00:40:32.120
Out of nothing.

00:40:32.120 --> 00:40:33.120
Out of nothing.

00:40:33.120 --> 00:40:37.120
Now you understand why the hachamim are so precise.

00:40:37.120 --> 00:40:42.480
Yes, the universe is a book, and God is the writer.

00:40:43.560 --> 00:40:45.240
There cannot be any relationship.

00:40:45.540 --> 00:40:47.220
That is the way God writes.

00:40:48.320 --> 00:40:52.960
We are the heroes of Israel.

00:40:53.440 --> 00:40:55.180
You know?

00:40:55.680 --> 00:40:59.200
And when he doesn't like the goyim, what he does?

00:40:59.840 --> 00:41:00.860
He doesn't kill them.

00:41:01.540 --> 00:41:02.260
Mahiti.

00:41:02.720 --> 00:41:04.840
He erases the name.

00:41:04.840 --> 00:41:10.840
He erases like a writer. I wrote this character, I don't like this character.

00:41:10.840 --> 00:41:16.840
Out! Out! Press delete. Out!

00:41:16.840 --> 00:41:22.840
It's terribly interesting. All the theology that is so difficult, how, what does it mean?

00:41:22.840 --> 00:41:28.840
Something out of nothing. Once that you take the book as a model, you know, every writer

00:41:28.840 --> 00:41:29.620
when you write.

00:41:30.920 --> 00:41:32.560
You're writing, again,

00:41:32.740 --> 00:41:34.320
Shakespeare's, yes,

00:41:35.320 --> 00:41:36.560
and Macbeth.

00:41:39.440 --> 00:41:40.700
But then comes

00:41:40.700 --> 00:41:41.420
another point.

00:41:43.920 --> 00:41:44.800
Can Shakespeare

00:41:44.800 --> 00:41:45.900
understand Hamlet?

00:41:50.900 --> 00:41:52.660
Can Hamlet understand

00:41:52.660 --> 00:41:53.160
Shakespeare?

00:41:53.160 --> 00:42:00.160
Can Romeo understand Shakespeare?

00:42:00.160 --> 00:42:04.160
Can Juliet understand Shakespeare?

00:42:04.160 --> 00:42:06.160
Not in a trillion years.

00:42:06.160 --> 00:42:13.160
Can Shakespeare understand Amlet and Romeo and Juliet and Magritte and Henry VIII?

00:42:13.160 --> 00:42:16.160
Yes.

00:42:16.160 --> 00:42:31.160
Is the life of Mr. Shakespeare similar in reality than the life of, again, Romeo and Juliet?

